From: vyos-ls1046a-build CI <ci@local>
Date: Sun, 04 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fman_pcd: point ENQUEUE_PKT word2 at an owned frag-info block (stop DMA CAM writes)

Every ehash HIT record wrote the ENQUEUE_PKT param word2
(dscp_fq_enable:8 | muram_frag_param_addr:24) as 0. The microcode
updates the ucode frag-info block at that MURAM address on every
offloaded frame, so with 0 it wrote counters into MURAM 0x0-0xf, which
is the FMan DMA CAM (FMDMEBCR = 0x00000000, fman->cam_offset is the
first MURAM allocation). Measured on .185 (2026-10-04, 6.18.54-vyos):
MURAM +0x4 / +0xc static when idle; +3,997 / +6,059,452 over a 1516 B
VLAN stream (exactly 1516.0 B per frame); ~840K/s at 9.4 Gbit/s routed.
This hits the shipping routed path, not only VLAN.

The vendor never writes word2 = 0: create_enque_hm() always stores
MURAM_VIRT_TO_PHYS_ADDR(dscp_fq_map_ff_g.muram_addr), a 32-byte-aligned
cdx_ucode_frag_info_t allocated once at init (cdx_ehash.c:138,3018).
ENQ's stats_ptr may legitimately stay 0 (vendor writes 0 without
INCLUDE_ETHER_IFSTATS), so it is left alone.

Fix: grow the existing FE internal-buffer reservation
(fman_pcd_ehash_int_buf_get/put) by a 32-byte zeroed block, record its
offset as pcd->fe_frag_off, and write it into word2. Every ehash table
holds an int-buf reference from creation, so any table that can take a
record has a non-zero block, and the block shares the int-buf
refcounted lifetime: muram_budget still returns to baseline on
disengage. Zero-initialised, so the options the ucode reads are the
same zeros it previously read from the CAM.
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
index 2fdf156..14566a1 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
@@ -200,6 +200,7 @@ struct fman_pcd {
 	unsigned long fe_int_buf_raw_off; /* unaligned off handed to free() */
 	size_t fe_int_buf_raw_size;
 	int fe_int_buf_refcount;
+	unsigned long fe_frag_off;	  /* ucode frag-info block (ENQ word2) */
 	unsigned long fe_root_ad_off;	/* sec.5 FE_ENTER root AD (16 B) */
 	unsigned long fe_group_off;	/* F-171: CONT_LOOKUP group AD (16 B) */
 	unsigned long fe_group_mto_off;/* F-171: group match table (64 B) */
@@ -1815,6 +1816,15 @@ static const struct file_operations fman_pcd_fe_enter_fops = {
 #define FMAN_EHASH_INT_BUF_TOTAL \
 	(FMAN_EHASH_INT_BUF_POOL_SIZE + FMAN_EHASH_GLOBAL_MEM_SIZE)
 #define FMAN_EHASH_ALIGN		256		/* EN_EXTHASH_TBL_ALIGNMENT */
+/*
+ * Vendor cdx_ucode_frag_info_t (cdx_ehash.c:138), 28 B rounded to 32. Every
+ * ENQUEUE_PKT param's word2 (muram_frag_param_addr) must point at one: the
+ * microcode updates its counters per offloaded frame. With word2 = 0 those
+ * writes landed on MURAM 0x0-0xf = the FMan DMA CAM (FMDMEBCR = 0), on every
+ * routed and VLAN HIT [SILICON 2026-10-04]. Zero-initialised, so the options
+ * the ucode reads are the same zeros it read from the CAM before.
+ */
+#define FMAN_EHASH_FRAG_INFO_SIZE	32
 #define FMAN_EHASH_NODE_SIZE		16	/* en_exthash_node descriptor */
 #define FMAN_EHASH_BUCKET_SIZE		16		/* lf-5.4 {u64 h; u64 pad} */
 #define FMAN_EHASH_MASK_MAX		0x7fff		/* hash_mask_bits: 4-bit field */
@@ -1889,7 +1899,8 @@ static int fman_pcd_ehash_int_buf_get(struct fman_pcd *pcd)
 	}
 
 	/* Bounds-check before reserving (section 8.6 item 2). */
-	raw_size = FMAN_EHASH_INT_BUF_TOTAL + FMAN_EHASH_ALIGN;
+	raw_size = FMAN_EHASH_INT_BUF_TOTAL + FMAN_EHASH_FRAG_INFO_SIZE +
+		   FMAN_EHASH_ALIGN;
 	mutex_lock(&pcd->lock);
 	avail = pcd->muram_reserved - pcd->muram_used;
 	mutex_unlock(&pcd->lock);
@@ -1902,9 +1913,10 @@ static int fman_pcd_ehash_int_buf_get(struct fman_pcd *pcd)
 	aligned_off = (raw_off + (FMAN_EHASH_ALIGN - 1)) &
 		      ~(unsigned long)(FMAN_EHASH_ALIGN - 1);
 	v = (void __iomem *)(void *)(void *)fman_muram_offset_to_vbase(muram, aligned_off);
-	memset_io(v, 0, FMAN_EHASH_INT_BUF_TOTAL);
+	memset_io(v, 0, FMAN_EHASH_INT_BUF_TOTAL + FMAN_EHASH_FRAG_INFO_SIZE);
 
 	pcd->fe_int_buf_raw_off = raw_off;
+	pcd->fe_frag_off = aligned_off + FMAN_EHASH_INT_BUF_TOTAL;
 	pcd->fe_int_buf_raw_size = raw_size;
 	pcd->fe_int_buf_off = aligned_off;
 	pcd->fe_int_buf_refcount = 1;
@@ -1922,6 +1934,7 @@ static void fman_pcd_ehash_int_buf_put(struct fman_pcd *pcd)
 	pcd->fe_int_buf_raw_off = 0;
 	pcd->fe_int_buf_raw_size = 0;
 	pcd->fe_int_buf_off = 0;
+	pcd->fe_frag_off = 0;
 }
 
 /*
@@ -2486,7 +2499,10 @@ static int fman_pcd_ehash_add_key(struct fman_pcd_ehash_table *t,
 		*(r + enqueue_off + 3) = 0;	/* bpid; fragmentation is S2 */
 		*(__be32 *)(r + enqueue_off + 4) = cpu_to_be32(fqid & 0x00ffffff);
 		*(__be32 *)(r + enqueue_off + 8) = cpu_to_be32(0);
-		*(__be32 *)(r + enqueue_off + 12) = cpu_to_be32(0);
+		/* word2: dscp_fq_enable:8 | muram_frag_param_addr:24. Never 0
+		 * (see FMAN_EHASH_FRAG_INFO_SIZE): 0 = DMA CAM corruption. */
+		*(__be32 *)(r + enqueue_off + 12) =
+			cpu_to_be32(t->pcd->fe_frag_off & 0x00ffffff);
 		param_end = enqueue_off + 16;
 	}
 
